# LF for the repo-root check scripts, so a checkout under core.autocrlf=true does not rewrite them
# to CRLF. This is NOT for the Copilot build's sake: build-copilot.mjs's put() normalises every
# emitted file to LF regardless of what the source carries, so the export needs no help here.
# Written as a property of that SETTING, never of one machine: an earlier version of this comment
# asserted "this machine runs core.autocrlf=true" and went stale the day the global config changed.
# The matching `github_build/** text eol=lf` rule is gone: the build is no longer committed
# (docs/adr/0003), so git never stores or restores those files.
# rules/scripts/ and skills/*/scripts/ are copied the same way and are deliberately NOT covered here:
# widening the pattern would buy nothing (put() already normalises) and would churn those files'
# line endings on the next checkout.
scripts/*.mjs text eol=lf
